!! Markers, vocabularies, activation

Starting with v1.0.0-beta-1, Custom-Markup ships a vocabulary engine. Every marker is a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker`. Markers group into vocabularies via a `Vocab/<Name>` tag. Each vocabulary has a meta tiddler tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>> that names the marker-tag and supplies a caption.

!! Marker fields

|! Field |! Required |! Notes |
|`open` |yes |The literal opening characters: `°`, `»`, `/°`, `CUT TO:`. |
|`kind` |yes |One of `glyph`, `glyph-level`, `word`, `inline-pair`. |
|`close` |inline-pair |The literal closing characters. |
|`mode` |no |`block` (default for non-inline-pair) or `inline`. |
|`element` |no |HTML element name or `$widget` reference. |
|`end-string` |no |Custom terminator. Without it, block markers terminate at a blank line; inline at a newline. |
|`classes` |no |Dot-prefixed CSS class chain, e.g. `.wltc-degree`. |
|`attributes` |no |JSON object of extra HTML attributes. |
|`allow-symbol` |glyph |Default `yes`. Set to `no` to lock the prose-safe form (e.g. the `.` marker). |
|`legacy-kind` |no |Friendly name (`tick`, `degree`, ...) so the v0.x `\custom <kind>=<symbol>` pragma still resolves. |
|`order` |no |Sort hint for editor-toolbar dropdowns. |

!! Activating a vocabulary

Two ways to opt in:

# ''Type field'': `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs`. A startup-module patch keeps the tiddler as a single `.tid` file on disk.
# ''Pragma'': `\importcustom [tag[Vocab/Legacy-Glyphs]]` at the top of a tiddler.

Vocab/Default is always active. With no `;vocab=` parameter, only Default markers fire.

!! Shipped vocabularies

* ''Vocab/Default'' (plugin): `°` `.` `»` `›` (block) and `/° °/`, `❮ ❯`, `⠒ ⠶` (inline-pair).
* ''Vocab/Legacy-Glyphs'' (plugin, opt-in): restores `´` `≈` `¶` removed from Default in v1.0.0-beta-1.
* ''Vocab/Presentation'' (editions): Fountain-flavoured Reveal.js DSL with `PRESENTATION`, `CUT TO:`, `ANIMATE TO:`, `FADE IN:`, terminator `FADE OUT.`.

!! Listing active markers

The `cm-active-markers` filter operator returns marker titles active for a given tiddler.

```
[<currentTiddler>cm-active-markers[block]]
[<currentTiddler>cm-active-markers[inline]]
[<currentTiddler>cm-active-markers[word]]
```

Empty source falls back to Vocab/Default so a dropdown without an edit context still renders a usable list.

